# Copy to `secrets.properties` (gitignored) and fill in.
# Every value is optional: an empty key degrades the matching feature gracefully
# rather than failing the build.

# Live captions. This is a URL, not a credential — scheme and authority of the
# `:server` deployment that mints per-session Soniox keys, no trailing slash.
# Empty → this project's own deployment
# (TranscriptionSecrets.DEFAULT_SONIOX_TOKEN_URL), so captions work in a fresh
# clone with nothing set here. Set it to point a fork at its own service.
#
# The Soniox API key itself deliberately does NOT belong in this file any more.
# Everything here is compiled into the shipped app — dex constants on Android,
# Info.plist on iOS, the JS bundle on web — so a provider key placed here is a
# provider key published to every user. It belongs only in the server's
# environment: `fly secrets set SONIOX_API_KEY=…`. See server/README.md.
SONIOX_TOKEN_URL=

# Discord / Apollo gate. Neither value is a secret — the client id is public by
# design and the guild id is a snowflake — but they live here so a fork points at
# its own Discord application. Empty DISCORD_CLIENT_ID disables the gate.
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
# Empty → falls back to matching the guild *name* "Apollo", which is convenient
# for a first run but not unique on Discord.
APOLLO_GUILD_ID=

# The stream server every playlist URL is built from: scheme + authority, no
# trailing slash (e.g. https://your-host.example:443). Deliberately absent from
# the source tree, so a public repository never carries it. Empty → the feed
# resolves nowhere and comes back empty.
#
# This is not a credential and cannot be one: a host the client streams from is
# on the wire and inside the binary (a web build ships it in the bundle). Keeping
# it here keeps it out of the repo and its history — that is the whole claim.
STREAM_HOST=

# Extra videos appended to the video feed: the raw URL of a plain-text manifest,
# one playlist URL per line (see docs/extra-videos.example.txt). A *secret* gist
# works well — it keeps the list out of this repository and lets you change it
# without shipping a release. Empty → the feed is exactly the numbered events.
#
# A secret gist is unlisted, not access-controlled: anyone with this URL can read
# it, and the URL ships inside the app, where it is extractable. Use signed URLs
# or a backend that authorizes each viewer if the recordings need real privacy.
EXTRA_VIDEOS_URL=
